# The member of latex's twelve that needs a rule the other eleven do not, and
# the only one worth measuring: in the corpus's `ltnews01.tex` a single
# `\iffalse … \fi` block is 990 bytes, 18.9% of the file, where the two
# verbatim bodies together are 127.
#
# So the string widening alone would have seated eleven members, collected the
# 127 bytes, and reported a family done.
#
# `\fi` closes on `is_command_name`: the keyword must be followed by something
# that cannot continue a control-word, which is why `\fixed` does not end an
# `\iffalse`. `\undefined{x}` is in the body to hold the other half - it is a
# control word latex has no rule for, so a run that was not raw would wall on
# it, and the `\section{a}` after `\fi` proves the run ENDED rather than
# swallowing the rest of the file.
#
# Claims are tree-sitter's tree: a `block_comment` over [0, 26) whose interior
# is one `comment`, and a live `section` after it.
roots 1
mends 0
holds block_comment
holds section
lacks ERROR
spans block_comment 0 26
spans comment 8 23
spans section 27 38
